[{"page": 1, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-1", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "T9. Cyclodextrin Chemistry", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 150.9783477783203, 271.1499938964844, 172.68597412109375]}, {"text": "7%", "bbox": [290.6499938964844, 193.6215057373047, 304.6280822753906, 207.18873596191406]}, {"text": "9.1", "bbox": [139.8509979248047, 209.5625, 153.9159698486328, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.2", "bbox": [171.47698974609375, 209.5625, 185.54197692871094, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.3", "bbox": [203.10299682617188, 209.5625, 217.16798400878906, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.4", "bbox": [234.72900390625, 209.5625, 248.7939910888672, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.5", "bbox": [266.35498046875, 209.5625, 280.4199523925781, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.6", "bbox": [297.98101806640625, 209.5625, 312.0459899902344, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.7", "bbox": [329.60699462890625, 209.5625, 343.6719665527344, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.8", "bbox": [361.2330017089844, 209.5625, 375.2979736328125, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.9", "bbox": [394.06500244140625, 209.5625, 408.1299743652344, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "∑", "bbox": [438.01800537109375, 209.5625, 444.3030090332031, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [144.03500366210938, 225.50250244140625, 149.7313995361328, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "6", "bbox": [175.6610107421875, 225.50250244140625, 181.35740661621094, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "8", "bbox": [207.28700256347656, 225.50250244140625, 212.9833984375, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "3", "bbox": [238.91299438476562, 225.50250244140625, 244.60939025878906, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [270.53900146484375, 225.50250244140625, 276.2353820800781, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [302.16497802734375, 225.50250244140625, 307.8613586425781, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "6", "bbox": [333.7909851074219, 225.50250244140625, 339.48736572265625, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "18", "bbox": [362.5690002441406, 225.50250244140625, 373.9639892578125, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [398.2489929199219, 225.50250244140625, 403.94537353515625, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "53", "bbox": [435.4639892578125, 225.50250244140625, 446.8589782714844, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "Cyclodextrins (CD) are a family of cyclic oligosaccharides, consisting of glucose subunits joined by α-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 244.41796875, 538.5673217773438, 279.00811767578125]}, {"text": "1,4-glycosidic bonds. The three most common cyclodextrins (α-, β-, γ-cyclodextrin) contain 6, 7, and 8", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 271.28851318359375, 538.5916748046875, 284.8557434082031]}, {"text": "α-D-glucopyranoside units, respectively.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 283.2434997558594, 243.17364501953125, 296.81072998046875]}, {"text": "9.1", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 308.853515625, 92.84233856201172, 322.4207458496094]}, {"text": "Calculate the molar mass of β-CD. Assume M𝑤(glucose) = 180.16 g mol−1.", "bbox": [114.69254302978516, 292.2882385253906, 466.0906066894531, 330.1165466308594]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 308.77850341796875, 521.8193969726562, 322.3457336425781]}]}, {"page": 2, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-2", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "CDs combine macrocyclic properties with glucose chemistry, which was demonstrated in the synthesis of", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.576416015625, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "X. Primary and secondary hydroxy groups show different reactivity due to being a part of CDs. Stoddart", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 167.17449951171875, 538.5524291992188, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "et al. synthesised compound K, where only one OH group remained free per glucopyranoside unit.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 179.12950134277344, 516.9561767578125, 192.6967315673828]}, {"text": "equiv.= equivalent", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 361.8929748535156, 142.06114196777344, 396.4831237792969]}, {"text": "9.2", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 399.77349853515625, 92.84233856201172, 413.3407287597656]}, {"text": "Tick the favorable chair conformation and draw the structure of K by complet-", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 399.77349853515625, 480.5821228027344, 413.3407287597656]}, {"text": "ing the CD template. Show stereochemistry unambiguously.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 411.7284851074219, 397.15728759765625, 425.2957458496094]}, {"text": "6.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 399.697509765625, 521.8194580078125, 413.2647399902344]}, {"text": "9.3", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 447.4435119628906, 92.84233856201172, 461.0107421875]}, {"text": "Determine the ring size, 𝑟𝑠, of macrocycle X. Give the number of stereocentres,", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 432.5279846191406, 480.5777893066406, 467.1181335449219]}, {"text": "𝑠𝑐, in X.", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 444.48297119140625, 149.76695251464844, 479.0731201171875]}, {"text": "8.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 447.36749267578125, 521.8194580078125, 460.9347229003906]}, {"text": "α-Cycloaltrin, a synthetic analogue of α-CD, was synthesised as follows.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 487.9804992675781, 387.7309265136719, 501.5477294921875]}, {"text": "9.4", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 683.0075073242188, 92.84233856201172, 696.57470703125]}, {"text": "Draw the structure of Y with stereochemistry by completing the CD template.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 683.0075073242188, 477.2498474121094, 696.57470703125]}, {"text": "3.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 682.9315185546875, 521.8194580078125, 696.4987182617188]}]}, {"page": 3, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-3", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "In 2000, Sinay et al. demonstrated that a single protic group (NH and OH) at unit 1 directs the next reduc-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.5855102539062, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "tive debenzylation of a primary OH group to unit 4 in the macrocyclic ring (or to unit 3 if the unit 4 position", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 167.17449951171875, 538.5855712890625, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "is not available). This allowed the synthesis of the following β-CD dimer as a mixture of constitutional", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 179.12950134277344, 538.5921020507812, 192.6967315673828]}, {"text": "linkage isomers.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 191.0854949951172, 133.08688354492188, 204.65272521972656]}, {"text": "9.5", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 483.9095153808594, 92.84233856201172, 497.47674560546875]}, {"text": "Draw the structure of L on the β-CD template. Fill in all the boxes.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 483.9095153808594, 425.138427734375, 497.47674560546875]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 483.8335266113281, 521.8194580078125, 497.4007568359375]}, {"text": "9.6", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 519.62451171875, 92.84233856201172, 533.1917114257812]}, {"text": "Determine the number of isomers of the β-CD dimer that can form during the", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 519.62451171875, 480.5594482421875, 533.1917114257812]}, {"text": "synthesis by Sinay et. al.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 531.5795288085938, 225.7979278564453, 545.146728515625]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 519.5485229492188, 521.8194580078125, 533.11572265625]}]}, {"page": 4, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-4", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "To confirm the positions of debenzylation, L was subjected to the “hexo-5-enose degradation” reaction,", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.59326171875, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "as shown below. The products were then analysed by mass spectrometry.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 167.17449951171875, 400.94134521484375, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "9.7", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 314.8265075683594, 92.84233856201172, 328.39373779296875]}, {"text": "Calculate the 𝑚/𝑧value for the two [M+Na]+ peaks that were observed for the", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 290.0081481933594, 480.5662536621094, 355.9605712890625]}, {"text": "degradation products from L. Use integer values of atomic mass.", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 326.781494140625, 418.6291809082031, 340.3487243652344]}, {"text": "6.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 314.75048828125, 521.8194580078125, 328.3177185058594]}, {"text": "Later, Sollogoub et al.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 357.4635009765625, 166.61175537109375, 371.0307312011719]}, {"text": "applied the ability of alkenes to direct the debenzylation to the “ortho”-", "bbox": [178.552001953125, 357.4635009765625, 538.5833129882812, 371.0307312011719]}, {"text": "glucopyranose unit for the synthesis of hexadifferentiated α-CD S:", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 369.4184875488281, 364.3966064453125, 382.9857177734375]}, {"text": "9.8", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 670.8364868164062, 92.84233856201172, 684.4036865234375]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of O-S on the α-CD templates. Fill in all the boxes. You", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 670.8364868164062, 480.5919494628906, 684.4036865234375]}, {"text": "may draw structures outside the boxes if appropriate. Assume 1,2-unit modifi-", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 682.79150390625, 480.5878601074219, 696.3587036132812]}, {"text": "cation happens clockwise, while 1,3-unit modification happens counterclock-", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 694.7465209960938, 480.5771179199219, 708.313720703125]}, {"text": "wise. Protic groups have stronger directing effects than alkenes.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 706.7015380859375, 416.9670104980469, 720.2687377929688]}, {"text": "18.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 670.7605590820312, 526.921142578125, 684.3277587890625]}]}, {"page": 5, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-5", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "9.9", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Determine the number of all possible arrangements of the functional groups", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 480.5634460449219, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "on a hexadifferentiated α-CD (assume only the CH2OH groups have been mod-", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 178.18450927734375, 480.56732177734375, 193.9508819580078]}, {"text": "ified).", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 190.1405029296875, 140.66415405273438, 203.70773315429688]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}]}]